      "text" : "We need four club tricks alongside two diamonds, two hearts and the spade ace. Play a low diamond and win in hand, then cash the club ace, preserving dummy's heart king as an entry. If both defenders follow, lead to the club queen and continue clubs, conceding one trick if necessary; even a 4-1 split supplies four club winners. Establish these before cashing the side-suit winners. If East shows five clubs, lead a second club low from both hands, conceding immediately; subsequently enter dummy with the heart king, cash the club queen and lead through East toward K8, establishing four club tricks in total. If West shows five clubs, lead toward dummy's Q7: play the seven over a low card or cover a higher card with the queen, then continue clubs to establish four tricks with at most one concession. Keep side-suit controls until clubs are established, and use the remaining diamond winner or heart ace to regain South as needed. Cash nine winners once available; do not risk the contract for an overtrick.",
